        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/7feea3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-26T15:56:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I apologize if this was already discussed, but I couldn't find anything similar with the Search tool</p><p>So I was reading through&nbsp;http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/files/sotm_rules_and_clarifications.pdf and I noticed a note about the Operative: since she misses the Villain keyword, she is not a Villain Character, just a Character</p><p>Now, does this change how various effects interact with her? I'm thinking chiefly about Legacy's Lead from the Front, which allows redirection from a \"Villain card\"... can he tank damage from the Operative?</p><p>There's also various Environment and Hero cards that specifically call out to Villain targets; is hte Operative eligible for those?</p><p>I was under the impression that any card coming with/from a Villain deck was to be considerd a Villain card by default, and that's also how I always played the Operative (and all cards in any Villain deck, since they are not thusly keyworded)</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:55.607Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
